1
00:00:16,271 --> 00:00:21,056
[SPEAKER_04]: So, is there any specific questions or any surprise questions?

2
00:00:27,483 --> 00:00:32,349
[SPEAKER_04]: So, we thought to bring up this sutta called the Relay Chariots.

3
00:00:35,107 --> 00:00:45,911
[SPEAKER_04]: And it's where Venerable Sariputta, he hears of a monk praised by other monks, and so he decides to go and visit him.

4
00:00:46,292 --> 00:00:48,412
[SPEAKER_04]: And his name is Venerable Puñña.

5
00:00:51,234 --> 00:00:56,896
[SPEAKER_04]: So, he eventually finds Venerable Puñña and then asks him a few questions.

6
00:01:02,232 --> 00:01:06,814
[SPEAKER_04]: He says, my friend, is the holy life lived under the blessed one?

7
00:01:07,715 --> 00:01:09,095
[SPEAKER_05]: And pañña replies, yes.

8
00:01:11,357 --> 00:01:16,259
[SPEAKER_04]: Is the holy life lived under the blessed one for the sake of purity in terms of virtue?

9
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:20,041
[SPEAKER_04]: He says, no, that's not the case.

10
00:01:24,283 --> 00:01:27,485
[SPEAKER_04]: Then, is the holy life lived for the sake of purity in terms of mind?

11
00:01:28,085 --> 00:01:28,265
[SPEAKER_05]: No.

12
00:01:30,308 --> 00:01:30,368
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

13
00:01:30,428 --> 00:01:30,588
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

14
00:01:30,608 --> 00:01:30,728
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

15
00:01:30,748 --> 00:01:30,908
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

16
00:01:31,128 --> 00:01:31,348
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

17
00:01:31,428 --> 00:01:31,528
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

18
00:01:31,548 --> 00:01:31,668
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

19
00:01:31,728 --> 00:01:31,968
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

20
00:01:32,469 --> 00:01:32,649
[SPEAKER_05]: No.

21
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:34,429
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

22
00:01:34,449 --> 00:01:34,509
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

23
00:01:34,549 --> 00:01:34,629
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

24
00:02:00,146 --> 00:02:03,629
[SPEAKER_04]: And for the sake of what, then, is the whole life lived under the blessed one?

25
00:02:04,069 --> 00:02:10,615
[SPEAKER_04]: It's about knowledge and vision, or whatever the utmost goal is, which is nibbāna, of course.

26
00:02:12,196 --> 00:02:13,137
[SPEAKER_04]: Virtue is not necessary.

27
00:02:13,978 --> 00:02:14,738
[SPEAKER_04]: We're just nibbāna.

28
00:02:15,899 --> 00:02:17,681
[SPEAKER_04]: Just let go of things.

29
00:02:17,701 --> 00:02:18,622
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll start at the end.

30
00:02:20,063 --> 00:02:21,744
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll have non-attachment now.

31
00:02:22,505 --> 00:02:23,706
[SPEAKER_04]: I don't care about things anymore.

32
00:02:26,023 --> 00:02:27,923
[SPEAKER_04]: Which is quite normal.

33
00:02:28,083 --> 00:02:29,504
[SPEAKER_04]: It's a quite normal view.

34
00:02:30,304 --> 00:02:31,224
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll just start at the end.

35
00:02:31,824 --> 00:02:32,924
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll be like an arahant.

36
00:02:35,285 --> 00:02:36,705
[SPEAKER_04]: But you can't get to the end.

37
00:02:37,165 --> 00:02:42,586
[SPEAKER_04]: You can't reach that destination without, you know, getting there, walking there, traveling.

38
00:02:45,827 --> 00:02:51,068
[SPEAKER_04]: So the simile that is given is the relay chariots.

39
00:02:54,058 --> 00:02:58,921
[SPEAKER_04]: And this is the simile that Puññā is giving to Sariputta, so that he can understand what he's saying.

40
00:03:00,602 --> 00:03:02,823
[SPEAKER_04]: He says, So, my friend, I will give you an analogy.

41
00:03:03,584 --> 00:03:17,692
[SPEAKER_04]: Suppose that while King of Kosala was staying at Sarvati, some urgent business were to arise at Saketa, and that between Sarvati and Saketa, seven relay chariots were made ready for him.

42
00:03:18,639 --> 00:03:23,300
[SPEAKER_04]: Coming out of the door of the inner palace in Sarvati, he would get in the first relay chariot.

43
00:03:24,041 --> 00:03:27,242
[SPEAKER_04]: By means of the first relay chariot, he would reach the second.

44
00:03:28,562 --> 00:03:32,523
[SPEAKER_04]: Getting out of the first relay chariot, he would get into the second.

45
00:03:33,384 --> 00:03:41,786
[SPEAKER_04]: And by means of the second, and so forth, he would, eh... Getting out of the sixth relay chariot, he would get into the seventh.

46
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:46,848
[SPEAKER_04]: And by means of the seventh, he would finally arrive at the door of the inner palace at Sargeta.

47
00:03:48,068 --> 00:03:53,072
[SPEAKER_04]: Complete dispassion, disenchantment, relinquishment, cessation, freedom from suffering.

48
00:03:53,092 --> 00:03:54,093
[SPEAKER_04]: That's the goal.

49
00:03:54,113 --> 00:03:56,495
[SPEAKER_04]: So, he doesn't practice for the sake of purifying the virtue only.

50
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:23,181
[SPEAKER_03]: But, without purifying the virtue, he won't be able to practice for the purification of mind.

51
00:04:24,521 --> 00:04:30,183
[SPEAKER_03]: Which means then, he won't be able to practice for the purification of views, for the purification of freedom from doubt, for the purification...

52
00:04:30,483 --> 00:04:35,284
[SPEAKER_03]: In other words, unless he starts with the first chariot, he won't be arriving at the goal.

53
00:04:36,504 --> 00:04:40,925
[SPEAKER_03]: So, none of the chariots are the goal, but without them, the goal would not simply exist.

54
00:04:42,393 --> 00:04:47,316
[SPEAKER_03]: And in the same sense, then, when the king did arrive, when they asked him, well, did you come by the means of this chariot?

55
00:04:47,356 --> 00:04:47,916
[SPEAKER_03]: He said, no.

56
00:04:48,976 --> 00:04:52,358
[SPEAKER_03]: I came by the means of chariot after chariot after chariot after chariot.

57
00:04:52,418 --> 00:04:53,019
[SPEAKER_03]: So, I'm done.

58
00:04:53,099 --> 00:04:54,159
[SPEAKER_03]: That's how I reached this place.

59
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,682
[SPEAKER_04]: They say, well, he abandoned the first chariot.

60
00:05:00,022 --> 00:05:00,222
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

61
00:05:00,663 --> 00:05:02,143
[SPEAKER_04]: So, he doesn't need his virtue anymore.

62
00:05:02,303 --> 00:05:04,144
[SPEAKER_03]: No, he doesn't need to purify it anymore.

63
00:05:04,765 --> 00:05:05,885
[SPEAKER_03]: It's his purity of virtue.

64
00:05:06,746 --> 00:05:11,008
[SPEAKER_03]: So, if you lack purity of virtue, you need to work on that chariot.

65
00:05:12,642 --> 00:05:15,263
[SPEAKER_03]: And if you don't like it, you can drop the work, i.e.

66
00:05:15,303 --> 00:05:18,243
[SPEAKER_03]: you can drop the chariot, because virtue now, it's there, developed.

67
00:05:19,103 --> 00:05:23,464
[SPEAKER_03]: So that's why it's purification of virtue that leads to the purification of mind.

68
00:05:23,484 --> 00:05:26,165
[SPEAKER_03]: You don't drop your mind either, when you finish with it.

69
00:05:26,685 --> 00:05:32,586
[SPEAKER_03]: But you can certainly drop investing further effort and work in purifying it, because it has been purified.

70
00:05:34,066 --> 00:05:35,887
[SPEAKER_03]: Polishing a brass plate or something.

71
00:05:36,367 --> 00:05:36,567
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

72
00:05:36,767 --> 00:05:38,827
[SPEAKER_03]: When it's clean and polished, well, stop polishing it.

73
00:05:39,728 --> 00:05:41,528
[SPEAKER_03]: I mean, you can carry on if you want to, but...

74
00:05:42,113 --> 00:05:42,973
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's then the question.

75
00:05:43,073 --> 00:05:44,033
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, so is that the purpose?

76
00:05:44,193 --> 00:05:45,854
[SPEAKER_03]: To just polish for the sake of polishing?

77
00:05:46,634 --> 00:05:46,974
[SPEAKER_03]: Ah, no.

78
00:05:47,214 --> 00:05:51,095
[SPEAKER_03]: It's to move on to the next one that needs now work on.

79
00:05:51,295 --> 00:05:52,135
[SPEAKER_04]: So...

80
00:05:52,255 --> 00:05:54,175
[SPEAKER_04]: So, you have to recognize there's further to go.

81
00:05:54,595 --> 00:05:54,795
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

82
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:58,776
[SPEAKER_04]: If you don't have the idea of where you're going... Yeah, yeah.

83
00:05:58,796 --> 00:06:03,337
[SPEAKER_03]: There has to be a unifying... like, you know, the king wanted to get to that other town.

84
00:06:03,357 --> 00:06:03,717
[SPEAKER_03]: That's it.

85
00:06:04,877 --> 00:06:07,558
[SPEAKER_03]: So, everything else was arranged to support that goal.

86
00:06:09,363 --> 00:06:24,228
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that is... the whole point is to keep, as we always say, the reasons for practice, the intentions behind your actions, keep that in the mind, because then you know why you are keeping the virtue, why you're making the effort to be sense-restrained, why you're making... guarding of the sense doors and so on.

87
00:06:25,048 --> 00:06:33,271
[SPEAKER_03]: But if you ignore your goal, then it's just... it can become... this can become a goal in itself, which means you won't be purifying your virtue anymore.

88
00:06:34,131 --> 00:06:35,171
[SPEAKER_03]: You will be assuming it.

89
00:06:35,591 --> 00:06:37,052
[SPEAKER_03]: You will be holding it on the level of

90
00:06:38,027 --> 00:06:41,108
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, well, this practice is about worshipping the first chariot.

91
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:47,370
[SPEAKER_03]: It's about glorifying it, it's about riding every now and then, but never leaving it to go into the next one, i.e.

92
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:49,851
[SPEAKER_03]: never completing that work, never committing to it.

93
00:06:51,291 --> 00:06:58,833
[SPEAKER_03]: So, the purification of virtue is not something you just take on, on account of authority, or tradition, or teacher.

94
00:06:59,354 --> 00:07:00,534
[SPEAKER_01]: It's something you have to do.

95
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:09,321
[SPEAKER_03]: And when you do it, then you won't need an external authority, tradition or a teacher to tell you about virtue or not, because you purified it.

96
00:07:10,702 --> 00:07:15,486
[SPEAKER_03]: So, that's why purification of virtue has to lead you to the purification of the mind.

97
00:07:16,887 --> 00:07:23,453
[SPEAKER_03]: So, purification of virtue, that you have to do, have to purify, have to keep an eye on, have to develop.

98
00:07:23,993 --> 00:07:26,836
[SPEAKER_03]: Then, when the Buddha says, oh, he becomes accomplished in virtue,

99
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:38,188
[SPEAKER_03]: whereby no unwholesome states can cause fear in him, because he knows that his virtue is accomplished.

100
00:07:38,308 --> 00:07:40,249
[SPEAKER_03]: He knows he won't break the virtue.

101
00:07:40,269 --> 00:07:44,110
[SPEAKER_03]: It doesn't matter what comes, what challenges, what pressures him.

102
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,090
[SPEAKER_03]: That means accomplished in virtue.

103
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:51,251
[SPEAKER_03]: That means virtue has been purified to the to the degree necessary to move on to the second chariot.

104
00:07:51,651 --> 00:07:58,293
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why purification of that accomplishment, that virtue, results in factual samādhi, as we said before in quote to those other suttas.

105
00:07:59,153 --> 00:08:06,497
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, oh, my virtue is unbroken, it's accomplished, no fear, nothing can perturb my mind on account of... Would I do that or not?

106
00:08:06,517 --> 00:08:17,562
[SPEAKER_03]: Because you know what you will not do, and you've been practicing that diligently, ardently, and now, you recognize that, no, doesn't matter what comes, these things will not be done.

107
00:08:19,589 --> 00:08:24,131
[SPEAKER_03]: So, purification of the virtue, then, becomes accomplished.

108
00:08:24,771 --> 00:08:31,893
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's already the form of samādhi, which is, again, exactly why it would lead to, then, the second step of purifying the mind.

109
00:08:34,034 --> 00:08:38,535
[SPEAKER_03]: So, purification of virtue, of course, sense restraint, precepts.

110
00:08:39,195 --> 00:08:39,916
[SPEAKER_03]: Is there anything else?

111
00:08:40,016 --> 00:08:41,296
[SPEAKER_03]: Or is it just keeping the precepts?

112
00:08:42,256 --> 00:08:45,017
[SPEAKER_03]: Just adhere to the precepts and you're purifying your virtue.

113
00:08:46,658 --> 00:08:47,338
[SPEAKER_03]: Would that be enough?

